r#  1541  29  148
p: .
t. 
|  The word ethnomethodology means the study of members’
|  meth\-ods - the members of a given culture. For the purposes of our
|  study, the members consist of the social participants who constitute
.  the interactional setting of the family court, both as dispensers of justice (and their auxiliary agents) and as parents in search of legal redress


--- Sentence/switch
id: 4
r#  1542  29  149


--- Sentence//end
id: 4
r#  1910  33  70
p: .
t. 
|  Because we examine the methods of the members themselves, we prefer
|  to call this kind of sociological study a sociological inquiry rather than a
|  methodology, as the only methods to be studied here are those of the social actors themselves, who engage in the situated (i.e., produced within
.  the context of the interactional setting) achievement of social order

--- Sentence/end 
id: 4
r#  1911  33  71

--- Paragraph/end 
id: 2
