t. 
|  , who conducted this study, had been primarily querying the
|  interviewee about her access to affordable housing, public
|  assistance, and other practical service and support needs, the
|  mother used this occasion to socially constitute her own
|  particular circumstances as part of a system by asking the
|  researcher whether there were very many other mothers in her
|  situation. Thus, in asking for other mothers in her
|  circumstances, she chose to perceive her individual
|  circumstances as presupposing a larger system at work rather
|  than an instance of an anomalous set of events, even though at
