p: .
t. 
|  In trying to illustrate explicative transactions, Pollner demonstrates
|  how in case after case the judges’ work occurred in real time, in public,
|  with the consequences of any decision [for example, lenient rulings
|  for traffic violations] unavoidably feeding back into the session and
.  furnishing the conditions and context of subsequent decisions (p. 242)

