|  As family court litigation progresses, the locally managed (contextually relevant) definition of what constitutes a fit mother becomes
|  increasingly at variance with how maternal fitness is practically reasoned
|  by members of society (i.e., society outside the parameters of the family
|  court setting), until a family court judge’s definition of what constitutes
|  a good mother may become almost unrecognizable when compared
|  with the standards of society at large. This is why protective mothers,
|  having lost custody and visitation in the family courts, often encounter
|  incredulity from peers, neighbors or colleagues who cannot understand
.  why these good mothers lost their custody and/or visitation

