|  This is one reason why, when state and federal investigators have
|  tried over the years to uncover the causes of abuses of the family courts,
|  they have not been particularly successful. A great deal of the systemic
|  madness has all too often been contained in running records of protective mothers who seek relief from the courts; and these running
|  records, communicated orally, are selectively shared with an inner circle that fits the political purpose for the construction of the running
.  record in the first place

